    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on a predictive model for a new microlending product. we're trying to move beyond just standard credit scores and look at more holistic indicators for risk. i was thinking about including features that capture \"neighborhood stability\" or \"community cohesion\" to help predict default rates. from a quant perspective, how should we approach weighting these kinds of environmental/social factors in a risk model?",
