      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High commercial turnover and renter concentration are indeed strong, measurable proxies for instability and lower cohesion. High turnover often indicates economic uncertainty, while high renter rates can suggest lower long-term community investment among residents. You should calculate these features as ratios or standardized differences within specific geographic bins. Then, you test the predictive power of these engineered features in conjunction with your target variable (default) using feature importance scores.",
      "source": "target",
