    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see. my concern is that some of these metrics might end up creating unintended biases towards certain demographics. if we use those proxies, won't the model basically just be penalizing more diverse or urban areas where renting is the norm and there's more movement? how do you balance the need for accuracy in risk prediction with the fact that these 'stability' metrics might just be surrogates for racial or socioeconomic profiles of certain neighborhoods?",
